/* ---- a-base/00-tokens.css ---- */
/* ==========================================================================
   PLECTICS — Obsidian theme
   Casio scientific instrument × Xerox PARC workstation × academic wiki
   Build: python build.py   (concatenates src/*.css → theme.css)
   ==========================================================================

   00 · TOKENS
   Every module uses ONLY these --plx-* tokens (plus Obsidian's own
   variables, which are mapped from them here). No raw hex outside this file.

   PLECTICS SEMIOTIC STANDARD (short form, full text in STANDARD.md)
   ─ Colour carries meaning, never decoration.
       teal    identity, link, the active/selected thing, "you are here"
       slate   chrome: title bands, instrument casing labels
       ink     content
       red     error / failure / destructive — and nothing else
       amber   caution, draft, provisional
       blue    selection range / compatibility (canvas, editor selection)
       violet  formal objects (theorem family) — very low chroma
   ─ Line style carries epistemic status.
       solid 1px      fact, boundary, settled
       double 3px     formal object (definition, theorem) — a closed claim
       dashed         provisional, estimate, unresolved, not yet existing
       dotted         reference / pointer to elsewhere (links, footnotes)
       hatched fill   absent, negative, disabled
   ─ Marks.
       ■ filled square  complete / proven (∎)
       □ hollow square  open
       ▸ chevron        can expand        ◆ diamond  menu / more
       §                section            ¶ paragraph anchor
   ─ Labels are instrument labels: condensed caps, tracked +0.06em, small.
   ========================================================================== */


/* Caps headings / labels: Nimbus Sans L (Helvetica-class, Aperture signage feel).
   "PLX Caps": weights < 550 → Regular, ≥ 550 → Bold. Archivo ExtraCondensed was
   dropped: its caps sit high in the line box (user: "uncentered vertically"). */
@font-face { font-family: "PLX Caps"; src: local("Nimbus Sans L Regular"), local("NimbusSanL-Reg"), local("Nimbus Sans L"); font-weight: 100 549; font-style: normal; }
@font-face { font-family: "PLX Caps"; src: local("Nimbus Sans L Bold"), local("NimbusSanL-Bol"); font-weight: 550 900; font-style: normal; }

/* ---------- 1. Fonts ----------
   Shipped (embedded in b-layer/58-alto-fonts.css): Alto Garamond Condensed,
   Archivo, PLX Caps (Nimbus Sans). Every other name is used only if installed;
   see docs/FONT-LICENCES.md. */
body {
  /* Garamond for titles and headings — the academic voice */
  --plx-serif: "EB Garamond", "Apple Garamond", "Garamond", "Palatino Linotype", "Book Antiqua", Georgia, serif;
  /* Display Garamond for the article title and h1/h2: Alto Garamond Condensed
     (shipped, EB Garamond at 80 % width). EB Garamond keeps h3/h4, theorem
     heads and true small caps. */
  --plx-display: "Alto Garamond Condensed", "EB Garamond", "Garamond", Georgia, serif;
  --plx-display-weight: 400;
  /* Reading text — IBM Plex Sans: screen-tuned, IBM design lineage */
  --plx-sans: "IBM Plex Sans", "Archivo", "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
  /* Default reading text — Constantia (user choice; Microsoft ClearType serif,
     2005: screen-tuned, sturdy, period-appropriate). CMU Serif is an option. */
  --plx-reading: "Constantia", "CMU Serif", "IBM Plex Serif", Georgia, serif;
  /* Reading text, serif alternative */
  --plx-text-serif: "IBM Plex Serif", "EB Garamond", Georgia, serif;
  /* Interface — Archivo (shipped): a grotesque close in width to Univers */
  --plx-ui: "Archivo", "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
  /* Instrument labels — condensed */
  --plx-ui-cond: "PLX Caps", "Nimbus Sans L", "Arial Narrow", sans-serif;
  /* Early-Macintosh system face — graph node labels, occasional system labels */
  --plx-chicago: "ChicagoFLF", "Chicago", var(--plx-ui-cond);
  /* Small text: properties, footnotes, captions, descriptions */
  --plx-small: "IBM Plex Serif", Georgia, serif;
  /* Data, code, metadata (Berkeley Mono only if you own and install it) */
  --plx-mono: "Berkeley Mono", "IBM Plex Mono", "JetBrains Mono", "Fragment Mono", Consolas, monospace;

  --font-text-theme: var(--plx-reading);
  --font-interface-theme: var(--plx-ui);
  --font-monospace-theme: var(--plx-mono);
  --font-print: var(--plx-text-serif);

  /* Type scale (UI) — dense, like an instrument */
  --plx-fs-label: 11px;   /* condensed caps labels */
  --plx-fs-small: 12px;   /* metadata, counts */
  --plx-fs-ui: 13px;      /* tree, menus, tabs */
  --plx-track: 0.04em;      /* label tracking */

  /* Quotations: readable upright reading face; Garamond only for the mark */
  --plx-quote-font: var(--plx-reading);
  --plx-quote-style: normal;

  /* Collapse markers (semiotic §5): boxed minus = expanded, boxed plus = collapsed */
  --plx-mark-open: "⊟";    /* boxed minus: expanded */
  --plx-mark-closed: "⊞";  /* boxed plus: collapsed */
  --plx-mark-font: "Segoe UI Symbol", "Cambria Math", "DejaVu Sans", var(--plx-ui);
  --plx-mark-size: 12px;

  /* Geometry */
  --plx-r: 1px;             /* panels: essentially square (user: less rounded) */
  --plx-r-key: 2px;         /* keys/buttons: barely softened corners */
  --plx-cut: 7px;           /* chamfer: the small angled corner (Aperture signage) */
  --plx-cut-s: 5px;
  --plx-hair: 1px;
  --plx-row: 24px;          /* tree / list row height */
  --plx-gap: 6px;
}

/* ---------- 2. Palette — LIGHT ("Instrument Gray / Paper") ---------- */
.theme-light {
  /* Plectics teal (Drive identity: #045A5A #0F4545 #428585 #639696 #B3EAE8 #D6F0EF).
     Fixed by default; Style Settings → "Follow Obsidian accent" re-derives it. */
  --plx-teal:        #0a5c59;
  --plx-teal-bright: #2f7f7b;
  --plx-teal-deep:   #0f4545;
  --plx-teal-wash:   rgba(10, 92, 89, 0.08);

  --plx-case:       #d9dfde;   /* casing: ribbon, tab strip, status line */
  --plx-case-hi:    #e7ebea;   /* sidebar body, toolbars */
  --plx-case-lo:    #c9d1d0;   /* gutters between panes */
  --plx-paper:      #fafbfa;   /* note surface */
  --plx-paper-2:    #f1f3f3;   /* table headers, secondary paper (Drive cell fill #F1F3F4) */
  --plx-well:       #ffffff;   /* input wells */
  --plx-lcd:        #d3ece9;   /* selection / active row — Drive #D6F0EF */
  --plx-lcd-2:      #e6f3f1;   /* hover */
  --plx-lcd-ink:    #0f4545;
  /* readout displays: matte e-ink paper, not a glowing LCD */
  --plx-eink: #e8e9e4;
  --plx-eink-ink: #262a29;
  --plx-eink-rule: rgba(38, 42, 41, 0.22);

  --plx-ink:        #263031;   /* body text (Drive #434343 → teal-tinted) */
  --plx-ink-2:      #4b5656;   /* labels (Drive) */
  --plx-ink-3:      #526563;   /* muted (Drive #748D8D, darkened to ≥4.5:1) */
  --plx-ink-4:      #607170;   /* faint (Drive #C1CFCD, darkened to >=4.5:1 on paper) */

  --plx-rule:        #a4b2b0;
  --plx-rule-soft:   #c9d4d2;  /* Drive #C1CFCD */
  --plx-rule-strong: #5f6f6e;  /* Drive grid #818989 → stronger */

  --plx-slate:      #2e3d3e;   /* title bands */
  --plx-slate-2:    #3c4b4b;   /* Drive meta #3C4B4B */
  --plx-slate-ink:  #eef4f3;
  /* filled chips (form tags, label tabs): background + on-colour ink */
  --plx-label-bg:    #3c4b4b;
  --plx-label-ink:   #eef4f3;

  --plx-red:     #a8433a;  --plx-red-wash:    rgba(168, 67, 58, 0.08);
  --plx-amber:   #8a6014;  --plx-amber-wash:  rgba(160, 118, 30, 0.09);
  --plx-green:   #4f6e22;  --plx-green-wash:  rgba(79, 110, 34, 0.08);
  --plx-blue:    #34628a;  --plx-blue-wash:   rgba(52, 98, 138, 0.08);
  --plx-violet:  #5d5280;  --plx-violet-wash: rgba(93, 82, 128, 0.07);
  --plx-steel:   #55707f;  --plx-steel-wash:  rgba(85, 112, 127, 0.08);

  --plx-key-top:  #ffffff;
  --plx-key-bot:  #dfe5e4;
  --plx-key-face: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--plx-key-top) 0%, #f0f3f2 55%, var(--plx-key-bot) 100%);
  --plx-key-face-down: linear-gradient(180deg, #cdd6d5 0%, #dbe2e1 100%);
  --plx-band:     linear-gradient(180deg, #3c4b4b 0%, #2e3d3e 100%);
  --plx-hl:       rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

  --plx-raised:   inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 1px 0 rgba(15,69,69,0.10);
  --plx-pressed:  inset 0 1px 2px rgba(15,40,40,0.22);
  --plx-recessed: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(15,40,40,0.09);
  --plx-float:    0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.05), 0 6px 18px rgba(15,45,45,0.16), 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
  --plx-hatch:    repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 3px, rgba(15,69,69,0.08) 3px 4px);
}

/* ---------- 3. Palette — DARK ("Night instrument", rev 0.3) ----------
   Dark is its own object, not light inverted. Light = a paper document on a
   pale-gray instrument case. Dark = a lit display glass set into a black
   bezel at night: the CASE is darker than the PAGE (as on a real device),
   keys are black with printed legends, labels are black strips, and state is
   shown by LAMPS (lit edges, glowing dots) rather than filled cells.
   Identity stays Plectics teal so a link means the same thing in both modes;
   amber is caution + highlights + phosphor displays only. */
.theme-dark {
  --plx-teal:        #5bbfc4;   /* identity / lamp */
  --plx-teal-bright: #8ad3d6;
  --plx-teal-deep:   #c8eef0;
  --plx-teal-wash:   color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 10%, transparent);
  --plx-lamp-glow:   0 0 6px color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 55%, transparent);
  --plx-plate:       #2a2d31;   /* callout / figure plates: a lighter panel lifted on the glass */

  --plx-case:       #0d0e0f;   /* bezel: matte black */
  --plx-case-hi:    #121315;   /* sidebars: black, a breath lighter */
  --plx-case-lo:    #060707;
  --plx-paper:      #1b1d1f;   /* the lit glass */
  --plx-paper-2:    #222428;
  --plx-well:       #0b0c0d;   /* inputs: recessed into the black */
  --plx-lcd:        color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 7.5%, transparent);   /* active row: faint lit wash; the lamp bar carries it */
  --plx-lcd-2:      #222426;   /* opaque: the Instruments plugin flattens translucent tokens to solid white */
  --plx-lcd-ink:    #f2f4f5;
  --plx-eink:       #232528;
  --plx-eink-ink:   #e6e7e8;
  --plx-eink-rule:  rgba(230, 231, 232, 0.16);

  --plx-ink:        #e2e4e6;   /* soft white, never #fff on black */
  --plx-ink-2:      #b8bcc0;
  --plx-ink-3:      #8f949a;
  --plx-ink-4:      #767b81;

  --plx-rule:        #3a3d42;
  --plx-rule-soft:   #2a2c30;
  --plx-rule-strong: #6d7278;

  --plx-slate:      #0b0c0d;   /* bands are black strips with printed legends */
  --plx-slate-2:    #101113;
  --plx-slate-ink:  #e6e8ea;
  --plx-label-bg:    #0b0c0d;
  --plx-label-ink:   #c9cdd1;

  --plx-red:     #ec7468;  --plx-red-wash:    rgba(236, 116, 104, 0.12);
  --plx-amber:   #e9a650;  --plx-amber-wash:  rgba(233, 166, 80, 0.12);   /* caution */
  --plx-green:   #a9c77f;  --plx-green-wash:  rgba(169, 199, 127, 0.11);
  --plx-blue:    #7fa6f2;  --plx-blue-wash:   rgba(127, 166, 242, 0.14);  /* selection */
  --plx-violet:  #b9aee0;  --plx-violet-wash: rgba(185, 174, 224, 0.10);
  --plx-steel:   #a9b3bd;  --plx-steel-wash:  rgba(169, 179, 189, 0.10);

  /* black rubber keys, separated by a black gap, lit from above */
  --plx-key-top:  #27292d;
  --plx-key-bot:  #18191c;
  --plx-key-face: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--plx-key-top) 0%, #1f2124 60%, var(--plx-key-bot) 100%);
  --plx-key-face-down: linear-gradient(180deg, #0e0f11 0%, #16171a 100%);
  --plx-band:     linear-gradient(180deg, #121315 0%, #08090a 100%);
  --plx-hl:       rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.075);
  --plx-fill:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 72%, transparent);

  --plx-raised:   inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl), 0 0 0 1px #000, 0 1px 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
  --plx-pressed:  inset 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.8), 0 0 0 1px #000;
  --plx-recessed: inset 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
  --plx-float:    0 0 0 1px #000, 0 10px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.75), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
  --plx-hatch:    repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 3px, rgba(255,255,255,0.06) 3px 4px);
}

/* Chamfer helpers — clip one corner at a small angle.
   Use on FILLED shapes (bands, labels, tabs, keys); bordered boxes use
   .plx-cut-frame technique (border drawn by a background layer). */
body {
  --plx-clip-tr-on: polygon(0 0, calc(100% - var(--plx-cut)) 0, 100% var(--plx-cut), 100% 100%, 0 100%);
  --plx-clip-br-on: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - var(--plx-cut-s)), calc(100% - var(--plx-cut-s)) 100%, 0 100%);
  --plx-clip-tl-br-on: polygon(var(--plx-cut) 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - var(--plx-cut)), calc(100% - var(--plx-cut)) 100%, 0 100%, 0 var(--plx-cut));
}
/* Chamfers are OFF by default (user: "don't just slant everything");
   Style Settings → Surface → "Angled corners" turns them back on. */
body { --plx-clip-tr: none; --plx-clip-br: none; --plx-clip-tl-br: none; }
body.plx-chamfer { --plx-clip-tr: var(--plx-clip-tr-on); --plx-clip-br: var(--plx-clip-br-on); --plx-clip-tl-br: var(--plx-clip-tl-br-on); }

/* Follow Obsidian accent instead of fixed Plectics teal (Style Settings) */
.theme-light.plx-use-accent {
  --plx-teal: hsl(var(--accent-h), calc(var(--accent-s) * 0.7), calc(var(--accent-l) * 0.8));
  --plx-teal-bright: hsl(var(--accent-h), calc(var(--accent-s) * 0.7), calc(var(--accent-l) * 1.1));
  --plx-teal-wash: hsla(var(--accent-h), 40%, 40%, 0.08);
}
.theme-dark.plx-use-accent {
  --plx-teal: hsl(var(--accent-h), calc(var(--accent-s) * 0.5), 60%);
  --plx-teal-bright: hsl(var(--accent-h), calc(var(--accent-s) * 0.55), 70%);
  --plx-teal-wash: hsla(var(--accent-h), 40%, 55%, 0.12);
}

/* ---------- 4. Map onto Obsidian variables ---------- */
.theme-light, .theme-dark {
  --color-accent: var(--plx-teal);
  --color-accent-1: var(--plx-teal-bright);
  --color-accent-2: var(--plx-teal-bright);

  --background-primary: var(--plx-paper);
  --background-primary-alt: var(--plx-paper-2);
  --background-secondary: var(--plx-case-hi);
  --background-secondary-alt: var(--plx-case);
  --background-modifier-border: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --background-modifier-border-hover: var(--plx-rule);
  --background-modifier-border-focus: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --background-modifier-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --background-modifier-active-hover: var(--plx-lcd);
  --background-modifier-form-field: var(--plx-well);
  --background-modifier-error: var(--plx-red);
  --background-modifier-success: var(--plx-green);

  --text-normal: var(--plx-ink);
  --text-muted: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --text-faint: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --text-accent: var(--plx-teal);
  --text-accent-hover: var(--plx-teal-bright);
  --text-on-accent: #f4f7f5;
  --text-error: var(--plx-red);
  --text-warning: var(--plx-amber);
  --text-success: var(--plx-green);
  --text-selection: rgba(66, 133, 133, 0.24);
  --text-highlight-bg: rgba(214, 190, 90, 0.32);

  --interactive-normal: var(--plx-key-top);
  --interactive-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --interactive-accent: var(--plx-teal);
  --interactive-accent-hover: var(--plx-teal-bright);

  --color-red: var(--plx-red);
  --color-orange: var(--plx-amber);
  --color-yellow: var(--plx-amber);
  --color-green: var(--plx-green);
  --color-cyan: var(--plx-teal-bright);
  --color-blue: var(--plx-blue);
  --color-purple: var(--plx-violet);
  --color-pink: var(--plx-red);

  /* radii */
  --radius-s: var(--plx-r);
  --radius-m: var(--plx-r);
  --radius-l: 3px;
  --radius-xl: 4px;
  --button-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  --input-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --checkbox-radius: 1px;
  --tag-radius: 1px;
  --callout-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --embed-border-radius: 0;

  /* borders */
  --border-width: 1px;
  --divider-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --divider-width: 1px;
  --divider-color-hover: var(--plx-teal);
  --hr-color: var(--plx-rule);

  /* shadows */
  --shadow-s: var(--plx-float);
  --shadow-l: var(--plx-float);
  --input-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  --input-shadow-hover: var(--plx-raised);

  /* typography */
  --font-ui-smaller: 11.5px;
  --font-ui-small: 12.5px;
  --font-ui-medium: 13.5px;
  --font-ui-large: 18px;
  --line-height-normal: 1.6;
  --line-height-tight: 1.3;
  --bold-weight: 600;

  /* chrome */
  --titlebar-background: var(--plx-case);
  --titlebar-background-focused: var(--plx-case);
  --titlebar-text-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --titlebar-text-color-focused: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --titlebar-border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --ribbon-background: var(--plx-case);
  --ribbon-background-collapsed: var(--plx-case);
  --tab-container-background: var(--plx-case);
  --tab-background-active: var(--plx-paper);
  --tab-text-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --tab-text-color-active: var(--plx-ink);
  --tab-text-color-focused: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --tab-text-color-focused-active: var(--plx-ink);
  --tab-text-color-focused-active-current: var(--plx-ink);
  --tab-outline-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --tab-outline-width: 1px;
  --tab-divider-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --tab-radius: 0;
  --tab-radius-active: 0;
  --tab-curve: 0;
  --tab-font-size: var(--plx-fs-ui);
  --tab-font-weight: 400;
  --tab-font-weight-active: 600;
  --tab-max-width: 220px;
  --tab-stacked-header-width: 28px;
  --header-height: 34px;
  --status-bar-background: var(--plx-case);
  --status-bar-border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --status-bar-text-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --status-bar-font-size: 11.5px;
  --status-bar-radius: 0;
  --scrollbar-bg: transparent;
  --scrollbar-thumb-bg: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --scrollbar-active-thumb-bg: var(--plx-rule);

  /* navigation */
  --nav-item-size: var(--plx-fs-ui);
  --nav-item-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --nav-item-color-hover: var(--plx-ink);
  --nav-item-color-active: var(--plx-lcd-ink);
  --nav-item-color-selected: var(--plx-lcd-ink);
  --nav-item-background-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --nav-item-background-active: var(--plx-lcd);
  --nav-item-background-selected: var(--plx-lcd);
  --nav-item-padding: 3px 8px 3px 24px;
  --nav-item-parent-padding: 3px 8px 3px 24px;
  --nav-item-radius: 0;
  --nav-item-weight-active: 600;
  --nav-indentation-guide-color: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --nav-indentation-guide-width: 1px;
  --nav-collapse-icon-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --nav-collapse-icon-color-collapsed: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --nav-heading-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --nav-heading-color-hover: var(--plx-ink);

  /* modals / menus */
  --modal-background: var(--plx-paper);
  --modal-border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --modal-border-width: 1px;
  --modal-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --prompt-border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --prompt-border-width: 1px;
  --menu-background: var(--plx-paper);
  --menu-border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --menu-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --menu-shadow: var(--plx-float);

  /* editor content */
  --h1-font: var(--plx-display);
  --h2-font: var(--plx-display);
  --h3-font: var(--plx-serif);
  --h4-font: var(--plx-serif);
  --h5-font: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  --h6-font: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  --inline-title-font: var(--plx-display);
  --h1-size: 2.1em;   --h1-weight: var(--plx-display-weight); --h1-line-height: 1.15; --h1-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --h2-size: 1.65em;  --h2-weight: var(--plx-display-weight); --h2-line-height: 1.2;  --h2-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --h3-size: 1.32em;  --h3-weight: 600; --h3-line-height: 1.25; --h3-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --h4-size: 1.12em;  --h4-weight: 600; --h4-line-height: 1.3;  --h4-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --h5-size: 0.82em;  --h5-weight: 700; --h5-line-height: 1.4;  --h5-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --h6-size: 0.76em;  --h6-weight: 600; --h6-line-height: 1.4;  --h6-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --inline-title-size: 2.5em;
  --inline-title-weight: var(--plx-display-weight);
  --inline-title-line-height: 1.1;
  --inline-title-color: var(--plx-ink);

  --link-color: var(--plx-teal);
  --link-color-hover: var(--plx-teal-bright);
  --link-decoration: underline;
  --link-decoration-hover: underline;
  --link-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  --link-unresolved-color: var(--plx-red);
  --link-unresolved-opacity: 0.9;
  --link-unresolved-decoration-style: dashed;
  --link-unresolved-decoration-color: var(--plx-red);
  --link-external-color: var(--plx-teal);
  --link-external-color-hover: var(--plx-teal-bright);

  --code-background: var(--plx-paper-2);
  --code-normal: var(--plx-ink);
  --code-size: 0.86em;
  --code-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --code-border-color: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --code-border-width: 1px;
  --code-comment: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --code-function: var(--plx-teal);
  --code-keyword: var(--plx-violet);
  --code-string: var(--plx-green);
  --code-value: var(--plx-amber);
  --code-tag: var(--plx-blue);
  --code-operator: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --code-property: var(--plx-steel);
  --code-important: var(--plx-red);
  --code-punctuation: var(--plx-ink-3);

  --blockquote-border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --blockquote-border-thickness: 2px;
  --blockquote-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --blockquote-font-style: normal;
  --blockquote-style: normal;

  --table-border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --table-header-background: var(--plx-paper-2);
  --table-header-background-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --table-header-font: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  --table-header-size: 0.82em;
  --table-header-weight: 600;
  --table-header-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --table-row-alt-background: transparent;
  --table-row-background-hover: var(--plx-teal-wash);
  --table-cell-vertical-alignment: top;
  --table-selection: var(--text-selection);

  --tag-background: transparent;
  --tag-background-hover: var(--plx-teal-wash);
  --tag-border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --tag-border-color-hover: var(--plx-teal);
  --tag-border-width: 1px;
  --tag-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --tag-color-hover: var(--plx-teal);
  --tag-size: 0.8em;
  --tag-padding-x: 0.42em;
  --tag-padding-y: 0.05em;
  --tag-weight: 400;

  --checkbox-color: var(--plx-teal);
  --checkbox-color-hover: var(--plx-teal-bright);
  --checkbox-border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  --checkbox-border-color-hover: var(--plx-teal);
  --checklist-done-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --checklist-done-decoration: line-through;

  --list-marker-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --list-marker-color-hover: var(--plx-teal);
  --list-marker-color-collapsed: var(--plx-teal);
  --list-bullet-size: 0.3em;
  --list-indent: 2em;

  --embed-background: transparent;
  --embed-border-start: 2px solid var(--plx-teal);
  --embed-padding: 0 0 0 1em;

  --hr-thickness: 1px;
  --metadata-divider-color: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --metadata-label-font: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  --metadata-label-font-size: 11px;
  --metadata-label-text-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  --metadata-input-font: var(--plx-ui);
  --metadata-input-font-size: 12.5px;
  --metadata-input-text-color: var(--plx-ink);
  --metadata-property-radius: 0;
  --metadata-property-background-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --metadata-property-background-active: var(--plx-lcd);
  --metadata-border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  --metadata-border-width: 1px;
  --metadata-border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --metadata-padding: 4px 8px;
  --metadata-gap: 0;

  --callout-border-width: 1px;
  --callout-border-opacity: 1;
  --callout-padding: 0;
  --callout-title-padding: 4px 10px;
  --callout-title-size: 11.5px;
  --callout-title-weight: 700;
  --callout-content-padding: 6px 12px 8px;
  --callout-blend-mode: normal;

  --icon-size: 16px;
  --icon-stroke: 1.6px;
  --icon-s: 14px;
  --icon-s-stroke: 1.6px;
  --icon-xs: 12px;
  --icon-xs-stroke: 1.8px;
  --icon-color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --icon-color-hover: var(--plx-ink);
  --icon-color-active: var(--plx-teal);
  --icon-color-focused: var(--plx-ink);
  --icon-opacity: 1;
  --icon-opacity-hover: 1;
  --icon-opacity-active: 1;
  --clickable-icon-radius: var(--plx-r-key);

  --file-line-width: 46rem;
  --file-margins: 28px 40px;
  --p-spacing: 0.9rem;
  --heading-spacing: 1.6em;

  --graph-line: var(--plx-rule);
  --graph-node: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --graph-node-unresolved: var(--plx-ink-4);
  --graph-node-focused: var(--plx-teal);
  --graph-node-tag: var(--plx-amber);
  --graph-node-attachment: var(--plx-steel);
  --graph-text: var(--plx-ink);

  --canvas-background: var(--plx-paper);
  --canvas-dot-pattern: var(--plx-rule-soft);
  --canvas-card-label-color: var(--plx-ink-3);
}

/* critique P2.8: in light, link hover goes darker (contrast rises), not lighter */
.theme-light { --link-color-hover: var(--plx-teal-deep); --link-external-color-hover: var(--plx-teal-deep); }

/* plates (callouts, figures): light = white sheet on paper; dark overrides in §3 */
.theme-light { --plx-plate: var(--plx-well); }


/* ---- a-base/10-workspace.css ---- */
/* ==========================================================================
   10 · WORKSPACE CHROME
   Casing, ribbon, folder tabs, toolbars, keys, wells, menus, dialogs,
   status line, scrollbars, focus. The instrument body around the paper.
   ========================================================================== */

/* ---------- Base ---------- */
body {
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  font-feature-settings: "tnum" 0;
  background: var(--plx-case-lo);
}
.app-container { background: var(--plx-case-lo); }

/* Keyboard focus — one consistent instrument cursor everywhere */
body :focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--plx-teal) !important;
  outline-offset: 1px;
  box-shadow: none;
}

/* ---------- Title bar (custom frame) ---------- */
.titlebar {
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
}
.titlebar-text {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label);
  letter-spacing: var(--plx-track);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  font-weight: 400;
}
.titlebar-button-container.mod-right { background: transparent; }
.titlebar-button { border-radius: 0; color: var(--plx-ink-2); }
.titlebar-button:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); }
.titlebar-button.mod-close:hover { background: var(--plx-red); color: #fff; }

/* ---------- Generic KEY (Casio key cap) ----------
   Used by: buttons, nav action buttons, view actions, ribbon actions.        */
button:not(.clickable-icon):not(.checkbox-container):not([class*="iconize"]):not(.callout-copy-button):not(.excalidraw *) {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: var(--font-ui-small);
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  padding: 4px 12px;
  height: auto;
  min-height: 26px;
  transition: background-color 80ms, box-shadow 80ms;
}
button:not(.clickable-icon):not(.checkbox-container):not(.callout-copy-button):hover {
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised), inset 0 0 0 100px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10);
}
.theme-dark button:not(.clickable-icon):not(.checkbox-container):not(.callout-copy-button):hover {
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised), inset 0 0 0 100px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
}
button:not(.clickable-icon):not(.checkbox-container):not(.callout-copy-button):active {
  background: var(--plx-key-face-down);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed);
  transform: translateY(0.5px);
}
/* Call-to-action key — the "EXE" key: teal face */
button.mod-cta {
  color: var(--text-on-accent) !important;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--plx-teal-bright), var(--plx-teal)) !important;
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 60%, black) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25), 0 1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) !important;
}
/* Destructive key — red only for destructive */
button.mod-warning {
  color: #fff !important;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-red) 85%, white), var(--plx-red)) !important;
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-red) 60%, black) !important;
}
button:disabled, button[disabled] { opacity: 0.5; background-image: var(--plx-hatch), var(--plx-key-face) !important; }

/* Icon keys (toolbar buttons) — flat until hovered, then a key cap */
.clickable-icon {
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  padding: 4px;
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  transition: none;
}
.clickable-icon:hover {
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
}
.clickable-icon:active {
  background: var(--plx-key-face-down);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed);
}
.clickable-icon.is-active,
.clickable-icon.mod-active {
  color: var(--plx-teal);
  background: var(--plx-lcd);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed);
}

/* ---------- Wells (inputs) ---------- */
input[type="text"], input[type="search"], input[type="email"], input[type="password"],
input[type="number"], input[type="url"], input[type="date"], input[type="datetime-local"],
textarea, .search-input-container input {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  background: var(--plx-well);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-top-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-recessed);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
}
input:hover, textarea:hover { border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong); }
input:focus, textarea:focus, input:focus-visible, textarea:focus-visible {
  border-color: var(--plx-teal) !important;
  box-shadow: var(--plx-recessed), 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-teal) !important;
  outline: none !important;
}
input::placeholder, textarea::placeholder { color: var(--plx-ink-4); font-style: italic; }

/* Toggle switch → slide switch with a raised knob in a recessed slot */
/* Geometry comes from Obsidian's own toggle variables, so the knob is
   always positioned by the app; we only change sizes and surfaces. */
body {
  --toggle-width: 34px;
  --toggle-thumb-width: 15px;
  --toggle-thumb-height: 14px;
  --toggle-border-width: 2px;
  --toggle-radius: var(--plx-r);
  --toggle-thumb-radius: 2px;
  --toggle-thumb-color: var(--plx-key-top);
  --toggle-thumb-shadow: none;
  --toggle-s-width: 28px;
  --toggle-s-thumb-width: 12px;
  --toggle-s-thumb-height: 11px;
  --toggle-s-border-width: 2px;
}
.checkbox-container {
  background-color: var(--plx-case-lo);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-rule), var(--plx-recessed);
  transition: background-color 120ms;
}
.checkbox-container:hover { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-rule-strong), var(--plx-recessed); }
.checkbox-container::after {
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-rule-strong), inset 0 2px 0 var(--plx-hl);
}
.checkbox-container.is-enabled {
  background-color: var(--plx-teal);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 55%, black), inset 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
}
.checkbox-container.is-enabled::after { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 55%, black), inset 0 2px 0 var(--plx-hl); }

/* Slider — recessed bar, teal fill to the left of a framed square key.
   CSS can't read the value, so the fill is the thumb's wide box-shadow, clipped by
   the input (overflow: hidden). The fill is slightly translucent so the track's
   gradient shades it. Variant (Style Settings): .plx-slider-segmented = LCD cells. */
body {
  --plx-slider-h: 16px;
  --slider-track-height: var(--plx-slider-h);
  --slider-thumb-height: var(--plx-slider-h);
  --slider-thumb-width: var(--plx-slider-h);
  --slider-thumb-y: 0px;
  --slider-thumb-radius: 0;
  --slider-thumb-border-width: 0px;
  --slider-s-thumb-size: 12px;
  --slider-s-thumb-position: 0px;
}
.theme-light { --plx-seg-line: rgba(15, 40, 40, 0.22); --plx-fill: rgba(28, 128, 116, 0.86); --plx-slider-track: linear-gradient(180deg, #e9edec 0%, #cfd6d5 55%, #bcc5c4 100%); }
/* dark track (segmented sliders, 85-fixes): a recess cut into the scheme's own case
   (was a fixed warm-brown gradient that showed in every dark scheme) */
.theme-dark  { --plx-slider-track: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--plx-case-lo) 0%, var(--plx-well) 55%, var(--plx-paper-2) 100%); --plx-seg-line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
input[type="range"] {
  -webkit-appearance: none;
  appearance: none;
  height: calc(var(--plx-slider-h) + 2px);
  min-width: 80px;
  padding: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--plx-slider-track);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
  cursor: pointer;
}
body.plx-slider-segmented input[type="range"] {
  background:
    repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0 19px, var(--plx-seg-line) 19px 20px),
    var(--plx-slider-track);
  border-radius: 1px;
}
input[type="range"]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track {
  height: var(--plx-slider-h);
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}
input[type="range"]::-webkit-slider-thumb {
  -webkit-appearance: none;
  width: var(--plx-slider-h);
  height: var(--plx-slider-h);
  margin-top: 0;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  /* double frame (dark · light · dark) + the fill to its left */
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-ink-2),
    inset 0 0 0 2px var(--plx-paper),
    inset 0 0 0 3px var(--plx-ink-3),
    -2001px 0 0 2000px var(--plx-fill);
  cursor: grab;
}
input[type="range"]:hover::-webkit-slider-thumb { background: var(--plx-key-top); }
input[type="range"]:active::-webkit-slider-thumb { cursor: grabbing; background: var(--plx-key-face-down); }
input[type="range"]:focus-visible { outline: none !important; border-color: var(--plx-teal); box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.18), 0 0 0 1px var(--plx-teal); }
input[type="range"]:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: default; }
/* small sliders (Style Settings rows, graph controls) */
.setting-item-control input[type="range"], .graph-controls input[type="range"] { --plx-slider-h: 14px; }

/* ---------- Ribbon — a column of keys on the casing ---------- */
.workspace-ribbon {
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  box-shadow: inset -1px 0 0 var(--plx-hl);
}
.workspace-ribbon.mod-left { padding-top: 4px; }
.side-dock-actions, .side-dock-settings { gap: 3px; }
.side-dock-ribbon-action,
.workspace-ribbon .clickable-icon {
  width: 28px; height: 28px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  --icon-size: 15px;
}
.side-dock-ribbon-action:hover,
.workspace-ribbon .clickable-icon:hover { color: var(--plx-teal); border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong); }
.side-dock-ribbon-action:active { background: var(--plx-key-face-down); box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed); }
.workspace-ribbon-collapse-btn { margin-top: 2px; }
.side-dock-settings { border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule); padding-top: 6px; box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl); }

/* ---------- Splits & panes ---------- */
.workspace-split.mod-root { background: var(--plx-case-lo); }
.workspace-split.mod-left-split,
.workspace-split.mod-right-split { background: var(--plx-case-hi); }
.workspace-split.mod-left-split .workspace-tabs,
.workspace-split.mod-right-split .workspace-tabs { background: var(--plx-case-hi); }
.workspace-leaf-resize-handle {
  background: transparent;
  transition: background-color 120ms;
}
.workspace-leaf-resize-handle:hover { background: var(--plx-teal) !important; }
.mod-left-split .workspace-leaf-resize-handle,
.mod-right-split .workspace-leaf-resize-handle { border-color: var(--plx-rule) !important; }
/* gutters between root panes read as the instrument body */
.workspace-split.mod-root > .workspace-leaf-resize-handle,
.workspace-split.mod-vertical > * > .workspace-leaf-resize-handle { background: var(--plx-rule); }

/* ---------- TABS — Casio "Sheet1 Sheet2" folder tabs ---------- */
.workspace-tab-header-container {
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  padding-inline: 4px 2px;
  height: var(--header-height);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
}
.workspace .mod-root .workspace-tab-header-container-inner { padding: 4px 0 0 0; margin: 0; gap: 2px; }
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header::before,
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header::after { display: none !important; }
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header {
  margin-bottom: -1px;
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom: none;
  border-radius: var(--plx-r) 0 0 0;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
  padding: 0;
  /* Aperture-style angled corner: top-right cut */
  --plx-cut: 8px;
  clip-path: var(--plx-clip-tr);
}
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header .workspace-tab-header-inner { padding-inline-end: 10px !important; }
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); }
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header .workspace-tab-header-inner {
  padding: 0 6px 0 9px;
  gap: 5px;
}
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header .workspace-tab-header-inner::after { display: none; } /* old dividers */
.mod-root .workspace-tab-header.is-active {
  background: var(--plx-case-hi);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
  z-index: 2;
  padding-bottom: 1px; /* covers the strip's bottom rule → tab merges with view header */
}
/* active tab of the focused pane: teal key along the top edge */
.mod-root .workspace-tabs.mod-active .workspace-tab-header.is-active {
  box-shadow: inset 0 2px 0 var(--plx-teal);
}
.workspace-tab-header-inner-title {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: var(--tab-font-size);
  letter-spacing: 0.01em;
}
.workspace-tab-header.is-active .workspace-tab-header-inner-title { font-weight: 600; }
.workspace-tab-header-inner-icon { --icon-size: 13px; color: var(--plx-ink-3); }
.workspace-tab-header.is-active .workspace-tab-header-inner-icon { color: var(--plx-teal); }
.workspace-tab-header-inner-close-button {
  --icon-size: 12px;
  border-radius: 1px; padding: 1px;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
}
.workspace-tab-header-inner-close-button:hover { background: var(--plx-red); color: #fff; }
.workspace-tab-header-status-icon { color: var(--plx-teal); } /* pinned/linked marks */

.workspace-tab-header-new-tab, .workspace-tab-header-tab-list, .sidebar-toggle-button {
  margin-top: 2px;
}
.workspace-tab-header-new-tab .clickable-icon,
.workspace-tab-header-tab-list .clickable-icon { padding: 3px; }

/* Side-dock tab headers (Files / Search / Bookmarks …) — a row of small keys */
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header-container { padding-inline: 4px; }
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header-container-inner { gap: 2px; padding: 0; margin: 0; align-items: center; }
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header {
  height: 24px; margin: 0;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  padding: 0;
}
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header::before,
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header::after { display: none; }
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header .workspace-tab-header-inner { padding: 0 5px; }
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header:hover {
  background: var(--plx-key-face); border-color: var(--plx-rule); box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
}
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header.is-active {
  background: var(--plx-lcd);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed);
}
.workspace-split:not(.mod-root) .workspace-tab-header.is-active .workspace-tab-header-inner-icon { color: var(--plx-lcd-ink); }

/* Stacked tabs */
.workspace-tabs.mod-stacked .workspace-tab-header { border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule); background: var(--plx-key-face); }
.workspace-tabs.mod-stacked .workspace-tab-header-inner-title { font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--plx-track); font-size: var(--plx-fs-label); }

/* ---------- View header — the toolbar row under the tab ---------- */
.workspace-leaf-content > .view-header,
.view-header {
  background: var(--plx-case-hi);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  height: 32px;
  padding: 0 6px;
  gap: 6px;
}
.view-header-nav-buttons { gap: 2px; }
.view-header-nav-buttons .clickable-icon,
.view-actions .clickable-icon { padding: 3px; --icon-size: 15px; }
.view-header-nav-buttons .clickable-icon:not(.is-disabled),
.view-header-nav-buttons button:not(.is-disabled) {
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
}
.view-header-nav-buttons .clickable-icon.is-disabled { opacity: 0.35; }
.view-header-title-container { font-family: var(--plx-ui); font-size: 12.5px; }
.view-header-title { color: var(--plx-ink); font-weight: 600; }
.view-header-breadcrumb { color: var(--plx-ink-3); font-weight: 400; }
.view-header-breadcrumb-separator { color: var(--plx-ink-4); padding: 0 3px; }
.view-header-breadcrumb-separator::before { content: ""; }
.view-header-title-parent { color: var(--plx-ink-3); }
/* the paper starts here — inner hairline on the casing */
.workspace-leaf-content[data-type="markdown"] .view-content { background: var(--plx-paper); }

/* Sidebar "nav header" toolbar strip (Files: new note / new folder / sort …) */
.nav-header {
  background: var(--plx-case-hi);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
  padding: 4px 6px;
}
.nav-buttons-container { justify-content: flex-start; gap: 2px; }
.nav-action-button {
  padding: 3px !important;
  --icon-size: 15px;
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
}
.nav-action-button:hover { color: var(--plx-teal); }
.nav-action-button.is-active { background: var(--plx-lcd); box-shadow: var(--plx-pressed); color: var(--plx-lcd-ink); }

/* Sidebar panes: section labels, search fields */
.workspace-leaf-content .search-input-container input { height: 26px; font-size: 12.5px; }
.search-input-clear-button { color: var(--plx-ink-3); }
.search-params { background: var(--plx-case-hi); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft); }
.tree-item-flair, .tree-item-flair-outer .tree-item-flair,
.search-result-file-matched-text { font-family: var(--plx-mono); }
.tree-item-flair {
  font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--plx-ink-3); background: transparent;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.search-result-file-matches {
  background: var(--plx-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
  border-radius: 0;
  box-shadow: none;
  font-size: 12px;
}
.search-result-file-match:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); }
.search-result-file-matched-text { background: var(--text-highlight-bg); color: var(--plx-ink); padding: 0 1px; }

/* Backlinks/outgoing pane headings → instrument labels */
.tree-item-self.is-clickable.mod-collapsible .tree-item-inner,
.backlink-pane > .tree-item-self .tree-item-inner,
.outgoing-link-pane > .tree-item-self .tree-item-inner {
  /* (file tree keeps its own style in 20-file-tree) */
}
.backlink-pane > .tree-item-self,
.outgoing-link-pane > .tree-item-self,
.embedded-backlinks .backlink-pane > .tree-item-self {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: var(--plx-track);
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  font-weight: 700;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
}
.embedded-backlinks {
  border-top: 3px double var(--plx-rule);
  margin-top: 3em;
  padding-top: 0.5em;
}

/* ---------- Status bar — Casio status line ("Alg  Standard  Cplx  Rad  ▮▮▮") ---------- */
.status-bar {
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  border-radius: 0 !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
  padding: 0 4px;
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  gap: 0;
}
.status-bar-item {
  padding: 2px 8px;
  border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
}
.status-bar-item:first-child { border-inline-start: none; }
.status-bar-item.mod-clickable:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); color: var(--plx-ink); border-radius: 0; }
.status-bar-item .clickable-icon { padding: 0 2px; }
.status-bar-item.plugin-word-count,
.status-bar-item.plugin-editor-status { font-family: var(--plx-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0; }

/* ---------- Menus — Casio drop-down: white card, dark rule, inverse selection ---------- */
.menu {
  background: var(--plx-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  padding: 3px;
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
}
.menu-item {
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 3px 10px 3px 6px;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  min-height: 24px;
}
.menu-item.selected:not(.is-disabled):not(.is-label),
.menu-item:hover:not(.is-disabled):not(.is-label) {
  background: var(--plx-slate);
  color: var(--plx-slate-ink);
}
.menu-item.selected .menu-item-icon,
.menu-item:hover:not(.is-disabled) .menu-item-icon { color: var(--plx-slate-ink); }
.menu-item-icon { color: var(--plx-ink-3); --icon-size: 14px; }
.menu-item.is-warning { color: var(--plx-red); }
.menu-item.is-warning .menu-item-icon { color: var(--plx-red); }
.menu-item.is-warning:hover { background: var(--plx-red) !important; color: #fff !important; }
.menu-item.is-warning:hover .menu-item-icon { color: #fff !important; }
.menu-separator { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft); margin: 3px -3px; }
.menu-item.is-label, .menu-group-label {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--plx-track);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label); color: var(--plx-ink-3);
}
.menu-item-title { white-space: nowrap; }
.suggestion-container {
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong) !important;
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  background: var(--plx-paper);
}

/* ---------- Dialogs — Casio dialog with slate title band ---------- */
.modal-bg { background: rgba(28, 33, 35, 0.35) !important; }
.theme-dark .modal-bg { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) !important; }
.modal {
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  padding: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.modal:not(.mod-settings) .modal-header,
.modal:not(.mod-settings) > .modal-title {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 7px 40px 7px 12px;
  background: var(--plx-band);
  color: var(--plx-slate-ink);
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}
.modal:not(.mod-settings) .modal-header .modal-title { color: var(--plx-slate-ink); font-size: 13px; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.modal:not(.mod-settings) .modal-content { padding: 12px 14px; }
.modal:not(.mod-settings) .modal-button-container { padding: 0 14px 12px; margin-top: 4px; }
.modal-close-button {
  top: 5px; inset-inline-end: 6px;
  width: 22px; height: 20px; padding: 0;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: 1px;
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  --icon-size: 13px;
}
.modal-close-button:hover { background: var(--plx-red); color: #fff; }
.modal.mod-settings .modal-close-button { top: 8px; }

/* Settings window: vertical tabs like the Casio "Math1 / Math2 / Trig" side tabs */
.vertical-tab-header {
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  padding: 8px 0 8px 8px;
}
.vertical-tab-header-group-title {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--plx-track);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label); color: var(--plx-ink-3); padding-inline-start: 6px;
}
.vertical-tab-nav-item {
  border-radius: 2px 0 0 3px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-inline-end: none;
  padding: 4px 8px;
  margin-inline-end: -1px;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
}
.vertical-tab-nav-item:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); color: var(--plx-ink); }
.vertical-tab-nav-item.is-active {
  background: var(--plx-paper);
  border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  font-weight: 600;
  position: relative; z-index: 1;
}
.vertical-tab-content-container { background: var(--plx-paper); }
.setting-item { border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft); padding: 9px 0; }
.setting-item-heading .setting-item-name {
  font-family: var(--plx-serif); font-size: 1.25em; font-weight: 600;
}
.setting-item-description { font-size: 12px; color: var(--plx-ink-3); }

/* ---------- Command palette / quick switcher ---------- */
.prompt {
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  background: var(--plx-paper);
  overflow: hidden;
}
.prompt-input-container {
  background: var(--plx-case-hi);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  padding: 6px;
}
.prompt-input-container input.prompt-input {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: 14px;
  background: var(--plx-well);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong) !important;
  box-shadow: var(--plx-recessed) !important;
  padding: 6px 8px;
  height: auto;
}
.prompt-results { padding: 3px; }
.suggestion-item {
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 4px 10px;
  font-size: 13px;
}
.suggestion-item.is-selected {
  background: var(--plx-slate);
  color: var(--plx-slate-ink);
}
.suggestion-item.is-selected .suggestion-note,
.suggestion-item.is-selected .suggestion-flair,
.suggestion-item.is-selected .suggestion-hotkey { color: var(--plx-slate-ink); opacity: 0.8; }
.suggestion-note { color: var(--plx-ink-3); font-size: 11.5px; }
.suggestion-hotkey kbd, .suggestion-hotkey span, kbd {
  font-family: var(--plx-mono);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom-width: 2px;
  border-radius: 2px;
  padding: 0 4px;
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
}
.prompt-instructions {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  background: var(--plx-case-hi);
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label);
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  padding: 4px 10px;
}
.prompt-instruction-command { font-family: var(--plx-mono); color: var(--plx-ink-2); }

/* ---------- Tooltips, notices ---------- */
.tooltip {
  background: var(--plx-slate);
  color: var(--plx-slate-ink);
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-slate) 70%, black);
  border-radius: 1px;
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: 11.5px;
  padding: 3px 7px;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
}
.tooltip .tooltip-arrow { border-bottom-color: var(--plx-slate) !important; }
.notice {
  background: var(--plx-paper);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--plx-teal);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

/* ---------- Scrollbars — slim recessed slot, key-cap thumb ---------- */
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 11px; height: 11px; background: transparent; }
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-track,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft); }
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-radius: 1px;
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  min-height: 28px;
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover { border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong); }
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:active,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:active { background: var(--plx-lcd); }
::-webkit-scrollbar-corner { background: transparent; }

/* ---------- Empty state, graph, misc ---------- */
.empty-state-title { font-family: var(--plx-serif); font-size: 1.6em; color: var(--plx-ink-3); }
.empty-state-action { color: var(--plx-teal); font-family: var(--plx-ui); }
.workspace-drop-overlay::before { border: 2px dashed var(--plx-teal); background: var(--plx-teal-wash); border-radius: 0; }
.drag-ghost, .drag-ghost-self { background: var(--plx-slate); color: var(--plx-slate-ink); border-radius: 1px; font-family: var(--plx-ui); }

/* Pop-over (hover preview) — a floating sheet with a thin title band */
.popover.hover-popover {
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-float);
  background: var(--plx-paper);
}
.popover.hover-popover::before {
  content: "PREVIEW";
  display: inline-block;
  height: 16px;
  padding: 1px 14px 1px 8px;
  clip-path: var(--plx-clip-br);
  background: var(--plx-band);
  color: var(--plx-slate-ink);
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  font-size: 9.5px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
}

/* hotkey chips in the palette: key caps, not pills */
.suggestion-hotkey, .prompt .suggestion-hotkey {
  font-family: var(--plx-mono);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom-width: 2px;
  border-radius: 2px;
  background: var(--plx-key-face);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  padding: 0 5px;
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
}
.suggestion-item.is-selected .suggestion-hotkey { background: transparent; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.35); }

/* Dropdowns: keep Obsidian's chevron background-image; only recolour the face */
body {
  --dropdown-background: var(--plx-key-top);
  --dropdown-background-hover: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  --dropdown-background-blend-mode: normal;
  --dropdown-padding: 0 26px 0 9px;
}
.dropdown, select.dropdown {
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: var(--font-ui-small);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  background-color: var(--dropdown-background);
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule);
  border-bottom-color: var(--plx-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--plx-r-key);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-raised);
  height: 26px;
}
.dropdown:hover { background-color: var(--dropdown-background-hover); border-color: var(--plx-rule-strong); }
.dropdown:focus-visible { box-shadow: var(--plx-raised), 0 0 0 2px var(--plx-teal); }

/* ---------- Collapse markers: [+] collapsed / [-] expanded (semiotic standard §5) ----------
   Replaces every chevron (tree, headings, callouts, properties, panes). */
.collapse-icon > svg,
.collapse-indicator > svg,
.callout-fold > svg,
.tree-item-icon.collapse-icon > svg { display: none !important; }
.collapse-icon::before,
.collapse-indicator::before,
.callout-fold::before {
  content: var(--plx-mark-open);
  font-family: var(--plx-mono);
  font-size: 10px;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -0.06em;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.collapse-icon.is-collapsed::before,
.collapse-indicator.is-collapsed::before,
.is-collapsed > .collapse-icon::before,
.is-collapsed > .collapse-indicator::before,
.is-collapsed > .callout-title > .callout-fold::before,
.callout-fold.is-collapsed::before,
.metadata-container.is-collapsed .collapse-indicator::before,
.cm-fold-indicator.is-collapsed .collapse-indicator::before,
.is-collapsed .heading-collapse-indicator::before {
  content: var(--plx-mark-closed);
  color: var(--plx-ink-3); /* the glyph carries the state; teal only on hover (critique P3.14) */
}
.collapse-icon:hover::before,
.collapse-indicator:hover::before,
.callout-fold:hover::before { color: var(--plx-teal-bright); }
.collapse-icon, .collapse-indicator, .callout-fold { transform: none !important; }

/* Univers Condensed caps: its kerning collapses word spaces after capitals ("IS THE" → "ISTHE").
   Turn kerning off wherever the condensed caps face is used. */
.titlebar-text, .menu-item.is-label, .menu-group-label, .vertical-tab-header-group-title,
.prompt-instructions, .status-bar, .markdown-embed-title, .metadata-properties-title,
.workspace-tabs.mod-stacked .workspace-tab-header-inner-title,
.markdown-rendered :is(h5, h6, th), .cm-header-5, .cm-header-6, .cm-table-widget th,
.backlink-pane > .tree-item-self, .outgoing-link-pane > .tree-item-self,
.canvas-node-label, .canvas-group-label, [class*="plx-"], body { font-kerning: none; }
/* body: Style Settings puts plx- classes on body, so [class*="plx-"] turned
   kerning off for the whole interface (reading text sets it back, 30-reading).
   Listing body keeps that look when Style Settings is not installed. */

/* Boxed markers ⊞ ⊟: one style everywhere, always visible, light, spaced from the label */
.collapse-icon::before, .collapse-indicator::before, .callout-fold::before {
  font-family: var(--plx-mark-font) !important;
  font-size: var(--plx-mark-size) !important;
  letter-spacing: 0 !important;
  color: var(--plx-ink-4) !important;
  line-height: 1 !important;
}
.collapse-icon:hover::before, .collapse-indicator:hover::before, .callout-fold:hover::before,
.tree-item-self:hover > .collapse-icon::before { color: var(--plx-teal) !important; }
/* Obsidian fades some markers until hover (graph controls, settings, headings) — keep them on */
.collapse-icon, .collapse-indicator, .heading-collapse-indicator,
.graph-control-section .collapse-icon, .tree-item-self .collapse-icon,
.cm-fold-indicator .collapse-indicator { opacity: 1 !important; visibility: visible !important; }
/* space between marker and the title it controls */
.tree-item-self > .collapse-icon { margin-inline-end: 4px; }
.graph-control-section > .tree-item-self .collapse-icon,
.metadata-properties-heading .collapse-indicator,
.callout-title .callout-fold { margin-inline-end: 5px; }

/* Focus ring only on controls — never on whole panes, documents or the editor surface */
.markdown-preview-view:focus-visible, .markdown-reading-view:focus-visible, .view-content:focus-visible,
.workspace-leaf-content:focus-visible, .cm-editor:focus-visible, .cm-content:focus-visible,
.cm-scroller:focus-visible, .nav-files-container:focus-visible, .workspace-leaf:focus-visible,
.metadata-container:focus-visible, .canvas-wrapper:focus-visible, .graph-view:focus-visible,
[contenteditable="true"]:focus-visible { outline: none !important; }

/* ---------- Settings (Obsidian 1.15 grouped layout) — instrument panels ----------
   content area = casing; each .setting-group = a bordered paper panel with a
   slate legend chip on its top edge; rows are tight, divided by hairlines. */
.vertical-tab-content-container, .vertical-tab-content { background: var(--plx-case-hi) !important; }
.vertical-tab-content { padding: 18px 28px 40px !important; }
.setting-group { margin: 0 0 18px !important; padding: 0 !important; background: transparent !important; border: none !important; }
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading,
.vertical-tab-content > .setting-item-heading {
  border: none !important;
  padding: 0 !important;
  margin: 0 !important;
  min-height: 0 !important;
  background: transparent !important;
}
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading .setting-item-name,
.vertical-tab-content > .setting-item-heading .setting-item-name {
  display: inline-block;
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond) !important;
  font-size: 11px !important;
  font-weight: 700 !important;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-kerning: none;
  color: var(--plx-label-ink) !important;
  background: var(--plx-label-bg);
  padding: 3px 18px 3px 9px;
  border-radius: var(--plx-r) 0 0 0;
  clip-path: var(--plx-clip-tr);
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading .setting-item-control:empty { display: none; }
.setting-items {
  background: var(--plx-paper) !important;
  border: 1px solid var(--plx-rule) !important;
  border-radius: 0 var(--plx-r) var(--plx-r) var(--plx-r) !important;
  box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04) !important;
  padding: 0 14px !important;
}
.setting-group:not(:has(> .setting-item-heading)) > .setting-items { border-radius: var(--plx-r) !important; }
.setting-items > .setting-item {
  padding: 9px 0 !important;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft) !important;
  min-height: 0;
}
.setting-items > .setting-item:first-child { border-top: none !important; }
.setting-item-name { font-family: var(--plx-ui); font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--plx-ink); }
.setting-item-description { font-family: var(--plx-ui); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--plx-ink-3); padding-top: 2px; line-height: 1.45; }
.setting-item.mod-navigable:hover { background: var(--plx-lcd-2); margin-inline: -14px; padding-inline: 14px !important; }
.setting-item.mod-navigable .setting-item-control svg { color: var(--plx-ink-4); }
.setting-item-control .clickable-icon { color: var(--plx-ink-3); }
.setting-item-control > .setting-item-info { font-family: var(--plx-mono); }
/* slider value readouts and numeric fields in mono */
.setting-item-control .slider-value, .setting-item-control input[type="number"] { font-family: var(--plx-mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
/* settings search field at the top of the sidebar */
.vertical-tab-header .search-input-container input { height: 28px; }

/* settings legend chip sits directly on the panel edge */
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading { line-height: 0; margin-bottom: -1px !important; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading .setting-item-name { line-height: 1.25; }
/* readable UI sizes */
.menu-item, .suggestion-item { font-size: 13px; }
.view-header-title-container { font-size: 13px; }
.vertical-tab-nav-item { font-size: 13px; }

/* Caps labels: trim the line box to the capital height so text sits optically centred
   in chips, bands and tabs (CSS text-box, Chromium 133+) */
.setting-group > .setting-item-heading .setting-item-name,
.metadata-properties-title, .markdown-embed-title, .canvas-group-label,
.markdown-rendered pre[class*="language-"]::before, .titlebar-text,
.workspace-leaf-content[data-type="canvas"] .view-header-title-container::before,
.workspace-leaf-content[data-type="canvas"] .view-content::before,
.workspace-leaf-content[data-type="canvas"] .view-content::after,
.popover.hover-popover::before {
  text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic;
}

/* ---------- Scrollbars — Casio / Rhino: a solid gray thumb with arrow boxes ---------- */
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-track, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: var(--plx-case-hi); border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-ink-4) 70%, var(--plx-case));
  border: 2px solid var(--plx-case-hi);
  border-radius: 1px;
  box-shadow: none;
  min-height: 32px;
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover { background: var(--plx-ink-3); }
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button {
  display: block; height: 14px; width: 14px;
  background-color: var(--plx-case-hi);
  background-repeat: no-repeat; background-position: center; background-size: 7px 5px;
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button:vertical:decrement,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button:vertical:decrement {
  background-image: linear-gradient(to top right, transparent 50%, var(--plx-ink-3) 50%), linear-gradient(to top left, transparent 50%, var(--plx-ink-3) 50%);
  background-size: 4px 4px, 4px 4px; background-position: calc(50% - 2px) 50%, calc(50% + 2px) 50%;
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button:vertical:increment,
body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:single-button:vertical:increment {
  background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom right, transparent 50%, var(--plx-ink-3) 50%), linear-gradient(to bottom left, transparent 50%, var(--plx-ink-3) 50%);
  background-size: 4px 4px, 4px 4px; background-position: calc(50% - 2px) 50%, calc(50% + 2px) 50%;
}
body.styled-scrollbars ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:horizontal, body:not(.native-scrollbars) ::-webkit-scrollbar-button:horizontal { display: none; }
/* small panes (sidebars, menus) keep a slimmer bar without buttons */
:is(.workspace-split:not(.mod-root), .menu, .suggestion-container, .prompt-results) ::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 9px !important; }
:is(.workspace-split:not(.mod-root), .menu, .suggestion-container, .prompt-results) ::-webkit-scrollbar-button { display: none !important; }


/* ---- a-base/20-file-tree.css ---- */
/* ==========================================================================
   20 · FILE TREE
   File Explorer, plus the trees that share its row language: Bookmarks,
   Outline, Tags, Recent Files (plugin) and search-result file rows.

   Not styled here (owned elsewhere): tab headers, .nav-header /
   .nav-buttons-container (toolbar above the tree), ribbon, status bar.

   Contents
     1. Module tokens (icon palette — token references only)
     2. Rows: geometry, type, chevrons
     3. Tree connectors (├ │ └) + active-path tint
     4. Row states: hover, active, multi-select, drag target, focus
     5. Counters (File Explorer Note Count plugin) + root strip
     6. Row icons (Lucide masks: type, prefix sign, keyword) + Iconize + ext tags
     7. Shared trees: Bookmarks, Outline, Tags, Recent Files, Search
     8. Style Settings toggles: body.plx-no-tree-lines, body.plx-no-file-icons

   GEOMETRY (Obsidian 1.15, measured)
     Every .tree-item-self spans the full tree width: Obsidian writes an
     inline `margin-inline-start: -17d px; padding-inline-start: 24+17d px`
     (!important) for depth d. Seen from the item's own x (= X):
         X+2 … X+22   collapse marker box "[+]"/"[-]" (centre X+12)
         X+22         row icon (15px), name at X+43
     A child list (.tree-item-children) sits at X+12 and its items at
     X+17, so a child's X' = X+17 and the parent's chevron centre is X'−5.
     We remove Obsidian's border guide and keep the 17px step exactly
     (12px margin + 5px padding) so the inline offsets stay correct.
   ========================================================================== */


/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. MODULE TOKENS
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
body {
  --plx-tree-step: 17px;                 /* Obsidian's fixed indent per depth */
  --plx-tree-guide-x: -5px;              /* guide x relative to child item (X'−5) */
  --plx-tree-mid: calc(var(--plx-row) / 2);
  --plx-tree-line: var(--plx-rule);
  --plx-tree-line-path: color-mix(in srgb, var(--plx-teal) 75%, var(--plx-rule));
  --plx-ico-size: 15px;                  /* row icon box */
  --plx-ico-lead: -2px;                  /* icon at X+22, clear of the [+] marker */
  --plx-tint-file: var(--plx-ink-3);     /* file icon tint */
  --plx-tint-folder: var(--plx-ink-2);   /* folder icon tint */
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2. ROWS
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Rows run flush to the panel edges, like a list on an LCD. */
.nav-files-container {
  padding: 4px 0 24px 0;
}

/* The trees that share the row language. */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self {
  /* 24px pitch: 16px line + 4px + 4px, no gap between rows */
  align-items: center;       /* Obsidian uses baseline for files: icons would grow the row */
  min-height: var(--plx-row);
  margin-bottom: 0;
  padding-top: calc((var(--plx-row) - 16px) / 2);
  padding-bottom: calc((var(--plx-row) - 16px) / 2);
  line-height: 16px;
  font-family: var(--plx-ui);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-ui);
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
  border-radius: 0;
  border: 0;
  box-shadow: none;          /* old theme: outset bevels caused jitter */
  transform: none;           /* old theme: hover translateX — never move rows */
  transition: background-color 60ms linear;
}

/* Folders read as headings of their branch. */
.nav-folder-title {
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  font-weight: 500;
}

/* Top-level folders are the "sections" of the vault: a touch heavier, and
   a hairline above each one after the first (drawn as a background so the
   row height never changes). */
.nav-files-container > div > .nav-folder > .nav-folder-title {
  font-weight: 600;
}
.nav-files-container > div > .tree-item + .nav-folder > .nav-folder-title {
  background-image: linear-gradient(var(--plx-rule-soft), var(--plx-rule-soft));
  background-size: 100% 1px;
  background-position: top left;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
}

/* Name: never wraps, never collides with the counter (ellipsis instead). */
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-inner {
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: pre;
}

/* Collapse markers "[+]" (collapsed, teal) / "[-]" (expanded, ink-3).
   The global rule lives in 10-workspace; here the tree-specific geometry,
   with enough specificity to beat Obsidian's own "\200B" ::before.
   The box is widened to 20px and re-centred on X+12 (X+2…X+22) so the
   mono marker (~16px) sits centred on the parent spine: the spine drops
   straight from the "+"/"-" sign. */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self > .tree-item-icon.collapse-icon {
  top: calc((var(--plx-row) - 16px) / 2);
  width: 20px;
  height: 16px;
  margin-inline-start: -22px;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  opacity: 1;
}
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self > .tree-item-icon.collapse-icon::before {
  content: var(--plx-mark-open);
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--plx-mono);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 16px;
  letter-spacing: -0.06em;
  white-space: nowrap;
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
}
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self > .tree-item-icon.collapse-icon.is-collapsed::before {
  content: var(--plx-mark-closed);
  color: var(--plx-teal);
}
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self:hover > .tree-item-icon.collapse-icon::before {
  color: var(--plx-teal-bright);
}


/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3. TREE CONNECTORS
   Each child item draws its own piece of the tree, so the drawing is local
   and needs no knowledge of heights:

        parent ▾            ::before  — vertical guide through the WHOLE item
          │                            (its row and all its descendants), so
          ├─ child                     the line runs on to the next sibling.
          │    …descendants            Hidden on the last child.
          └─ last child     ::after   — "└": vertical from the item's top to
                                       the row middle, then the tick right.

   Ticks stop just short of what they point at: the "[+]"/"[-]" marker
   (folders) or the type icon (files). Lines are on z-index 1 so full-width hover /
   active rows never cut them.

   Virtualisation: Obsidian culls rows outside the viewport (+ a buffer), so
   the last *rendered* child of a long branch can briefly take the elbow
   while it sits off-screen. Accepted; it is invisible in practice.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children {
  /* keep Obsidian's 17px step exactly; drop its border guide */
  margin-inline-start: 12px;
  padding-inline-start: 5px;
  border-inline-start: 0;
}

:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item {
  position: relative;
  /* per-item knobs, overridden for the active path below */
  --plx-c-run: var(--plx-tree-line);     /* ::before, guide to next sibling */
  --plx-c-elbow: var(--plx-tree-line);   /* ::after, vertical half */
  --plx-c-tick: var(--plx-tree-line);    /* ::after, horizontal tick */
  --plx-c-tick-len: 25px;                /* X'−5 → X'+20: file → its icon (X'+22) */
}
/* folders: tick ends just before the "[+]" marker (X'+4) */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item:has(> .tree-item-self .collapse-icon) {
  --plx-c-tick-len: 8px;
}

:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item::before,
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 1;
  inset-inline-start: var(--plx-tree-guide-x);
  top: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  pointer-events: none;
}
/* │ run-on guide */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item::before {
  bottom: 0;
  width: 0;
  border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-c-run);
}
/* └ elbow + tick */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item::after {
  height: calc(var(--plx-tree-mid) + 0.5px);
  width: var(--plx-c-tick-len);
  border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--plx-c-elbow);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-c-tick);
}
/* the last child ends the branch: no run-on */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-children > .tree-item:last-child::before {
  content: none;
}

/* Active path (File Explorer only): the line from each ancestor's chevron
   down to the child that leads to the active file is tinted teal.
   - the branch child (contains .is-active): elbow + tick teal
   - siblings ABOVE it: their run-on guide (and elbow) teal
   Rendered rows are few (virtualised), so these :has() checks are cheap. */
.nav-files-container .tree-item-children > .tree-item:has(.is-active) {
  --plx-c-elbow: var(--plx-tree-line-path);
  --plx-c-tick: var(--plx-tree-line-path);
}
.nav-files-container .tree-item-children > .tree-item:has(~ .tree-item .is-active) {
  --plx-c-run: var(--plx-tree-line-path);
  --plx-c-elbow: var(--plx-tree-line-path);
}


/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4. ROW STATES
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self.is-clickable:hover {
  background-color: var(--plx-lcd-2);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
}

/* Active file = Casio list cursor: LCD row + 2px teal key at the left edge */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self.is-active,
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-self.is-active:hover {
  background-color: var(--plx-lcd);
  /* the key: 3px teal bar whose foot is cut at an angle (a small chamfer,
     like a Casio list cursor / Aperture sign marker) */
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(var(--plx-teal), var(--plx-teal)),
    linear-gradient(to bottom left, transparent 50%, var(--plx-teal) 50%);
  background-size: 3px calc(100% - 3px), 3px 3px;
  background-position: left top, left bottom;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  color: var(--plx-lcd-ink);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* Multi-select (shift/ctrl click): blue wash = a selection range */
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-self.is-selected,
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-self.is-selected:hover {
  background-color: var(--plx-blue-wash);
  background-image: linear-gradient(var(--plx-blue), var(--plx-blue));
  background-size: 2px 100%;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  color: var(--plx-ink);
}
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-self.is-selected.is-active {
  background-color: var(--plx-lcd);
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(var(--plx-teal), var(--plx-teal)),
    linear-gradient(to bottom left, transparent 50%, var(--plx-teal) 50%);
  background-size: 3px calc(100% - 3px), 3px 3px;
  background-position: left top, left bottom;
}

/* Drop target while dragging: dashed teal = "would go here" (provisional) */
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item.is-being-dragged-over,
:is(.nav-files-container, .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"]) .tree-item-self.is-being-dragged-over,
.nav-files-container.is-being-dragged-over {
  background-color: var(--plx-teal-wash);
  outline: 1px dashed var(--plx-teal);
  outline-offset: -1px;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.nav-files-container .tree-item-self.is-being-dragged {
  opacity: 0.55;
}

/* Keyboard focus: dotted inset frame (dotted = pointer to "here") */
:is(.nav-files-container,
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="bookmarks"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="outline"],
    .workspace-leaf-content[data-type="tag"]) .tree-item-self.has-focus {
  box-shadow: none;
  outline: 1px dotted var(--plx-rule-strong);
  outline-offset: -1px;
}

/* Rename in place: an input well */
.nav-files-container .tree-item-self .tree-item-inner[contenteditable="true"],
.nav-files-container .tree-item-self.is-being-renamed .tree-item-inner {
  background: var(--plx-well);
  color: var(--plx-ink);
  box-shadow: var(--plx-recessed);
  outline: 1px solid var(--plx-teal);
  outline-offset: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 0 3px;
  text-overflow: clip;
}


/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   5. COUNTERS — File Explorer Note Count plugin
   The plugin prints `data-count` through ::after. Restyled as a tiny LCD
   digit readout: mono, tabular, faint, right-aligned, never overlapping the
   name (the name ellipsises first).
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.nav-folder-title[data-count]::after,
.oz-explorer-root-nav-folder-title[data-count]::after {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  order: 9;
  margin: 0 0 0 8px;
  padding: 0;
  min-width: 3ch;
  text-align: end;
  font-family: var(--plx-mono);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-small);
  font-weight: 400;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums slashed-zero;
  letter-spacing: 0;
  line-height: 16px;
  color: var(--plx-ink-4);
  background: none;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.nav-folder-title[data-count]:hover::after {
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
}
.nav-folder-title.is-active[data-count]::after {
  color: var(--plx-lcd-ink);
}

/* Root strip ("VAULT ……… 398"): a Casio panel label above the tree. */
.nav-files-container .oz-explorer-root-folder {
  margin: 0 0 4px 0;
}
.oz-explorer-root-nav-folder-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  height: 20px;
  padding: 0 8px 0 10px;
  background: var(--plx-case);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--plx-rule-soft);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--plx-hl);
  font-family: var(--plx-ui-cond);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: var(--plx-track);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--plx-ink-2);
}
.oz-explorer-root-nav-folder-title .tree-item-inner {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.oz-explorer-root-nav-folder-title[data-count]::after {
  color: var(--plx-ink-3);
  font-size: var(--plx-fs-label);
}


/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   6. ROW ICONS — Lucide (the icon family Obsidian itself uses)
   Drawn by ::before on each title, before the name. Each icon is a Lucide
   SVG (ISC licence) used as a MASK, so its colour comes from tokens via
   background-color. Stroke re-set to 2.4/24 (≈1.5px at 15px) to match
   Obsidian's UI icons. One custom property per icon: --plx-ico-<lucide id>.

   Which icon a row gets — three layers, highest first:
     1. KEYWORD in the row's own name   → --plx-row-key  (+ --plx-row-key-tint)
     2. PREFIX SIGN on the row's name   → --plx-row-sign
     3. TYPE / DEPTH default            → --plx-row-icon (+ --plx-row-tint)
   and a real Iconize icon (svg/img) beats all three.

   Type defaults (by data-path suffix; later rules win):
     top-level folder  library          nested folder  folder / folder-open
     .md               file-text        .canvas        layout-dashboard
     .excalidraw(.md)  pencil-ruler     .base          table-2
     .pdf              file-type        images         image
     audio             file-audio       video          film
     code              file-code        json           file-json
     csv / tsv         sheet            .tex           sigma
     .bib              book-marked      anything else  file

   Prefix signs (Plectics filing standard):
     ~ META (asterisk; row quieter, ink-3)   _ support/assets (paperclip)
     @ people (user-round)                   ! pinned (pin)
     + inbox (inbox)                         % or = index / MOC (list-tree)

   Keywords (case-insensitive; "$=" = name ends with, for short words that
   would otherwise hit inside other words): Meta, admin, Sandbox, Recent,
   Maintenance, Template, Attachment/Assets, Inbox, Archive, Sticky Notes,
   Bases, Excalidraw, Empty (dashed circle, ink-3), Recycle Bin/Trash/Deleted
   (ink-3), Unfinished/Draft/WIP (construction, amber), Low Quality
   (circle-alert, amber).

   "Own name" matching: CSS cannot isolate the last path segment, so a
   sign/keyword rule only fires when the PARENT folder's title does not
   match the same pattern (otherwise every descendant of "~ Maintenance"
   would inherit the wrench). Limitation: "~y" directly inside "~x" keeps
   its type icon; same for a keyword repeated in parent and child.

